WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.290
Performance under pressure is different from performance in calm conditions.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:08.220
Pressure may come from time limits, uncertainty, consequence, audience, conflict,

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.200
or the knowledge that a decision matters.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.950
At a general level, pressure can sharpen focus for some tasks,

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.580
but it can also narrow attention, increase rushing,

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.920
and reduce decision quality if it is not managed.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.440
The goal is not to eliminate every sign of pressure.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.065
Real work often contains pressure.

00:00:22.065 --> 00:00:25.725
The goal is performance stability: the ability to keep observing, reasoning,

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.883
communicating, and acting in a useful way.

00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:29.850
Simple pre-performance routines can help.

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:33.950
A performer may review the objective, define the first action, check required resources,

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.840
and decide in advance when to slow down, escalate, or ask for support.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.690
Practical pause techniques can also help at a non-clinical level.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:43.000
Taking a brief breath, naming the next decision,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.510
or asking what evidence is missing can interrupt panic and tunnel vision.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.320
These techniques are not medical treatment.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.600
They are ordinary performance habits that create a small space between pressure and

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:52.400
action,

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.115
especially when the urge is to rush.

00:00:54.115 --> 00:00:57.675
Expert performers know when speed is useful and when slowing down is safer.

00:00:57.675 --> 00:01:01.800
If the situation is familiar and the action is reversible, speed may be appropriate.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.850
If the stakes are high, the information is unclear, or the action is hard to undo,

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.380
a deliberate pause can improve quality.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.085
Stability under pressure comes from preparation, routines, team support,

00:01:11.085 --> 00:01:13.850
and the willingness to adjust pace when the situation demands it.
